    "type": "numeric",
    "prompt": "The mean weight of a crate of 9 pumpkins is 16 pounds. One of the pumpkins is removed. The mean weight of the remaining 8 pumpkins is 13 pounds. What is the weight, in pounds, of the pumpkin that was removed?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": null,
    "answer": "40",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": "pounds",
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Totals",
        "body": "$9 \\times 16 = 144$ and $8 \\times 13 = 104$. Removed: $144 - 104 = 40$ pounds.\n\n**Answer: 40 pounds**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Effect on the mean",
        "body": "The 8 remaining pumpkins are each 3 lb below the old mean, a total of 24 lb below. So the removed pumpkin is 24 lb above the old mean: $16 + 24 = 40$.\n\n**Answer: 40 pounds**"
      }
    ],
